<title>SWEDEN: Ericsson signs $300 million deal with AT&amp;T.</title>
<headline>Ericsson signs $300 million deal with AT&amp;T.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM, Sweden</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish telecoms giant LM Ericsson AB said Thursday it had won an order worth two billion crowns ($303 million) for mobile telephone equipment from AT&amp;T Wireless Services.</p>
<p>Ericsson said this was the biggest order that Ericsson has signed with a U.S. buyer for mobile telephone equipment.</p>
<p>Under the agreement, Ericsson will supply digital PCS (personal communications services) equipment and other mobile telephone equipment starting in January 1997.</p>
</text>
